  "flags": [
    {"page": 1, "what": "A Brigand warband needs at least 3 models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported. No henchmen group sizes and no maximum profiles are printed, so the warband takes our Human race."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "The skill table prints no Special column, so the warband has no skill group."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "The Rapier, Halberd and Lance are the list's \"Fallen Noble Extra Equipment\" column: read as Fallen Noble only. \"(#) Denotes Heroes Only equipment\" marks the Heavy Armour, Barding and Crossbow, and the whole Miscellaneous Equipment heading, so the Horse and Warhorse are heroes only too."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "\"Rapier (TC 7)\" is our Rapier; the (TC 7) is the source the PDF cites, not part of the name. The Barding (60 gc), Horse (30 gc), Warhorse (60 gc) and Hunting Arrows (25 gc) are marked \"*Starting Price Only\": list prices are starting prices in the app, so no note is added."},
    {"page": 2, "what": "The Brigand list's Dagger is 2 gc with no \"first free\"; the Poacher list's is \"Dagger (first free)\". As printed."},
    {"page": 4, "what": "The Scarface's Horribly Scarred (he causes fear) is our shared Fear, under that name."},
    {"page": 4, "what": "The Fallen Noble's Knights Feats rule grants him the Knights Errant's skill list, so he learns from the Knights Feats group (declared in the Bretonnian Knights-Errant file for both types) and the rule itself is not imported: who may take a skill is never a warband rule. The group's note says he is the only Brigand who learns them."},
    {"page": 6, "what": "The Green Jack's Weapons/Armour line reads \"A Likely Lad may be equipped from the Poacher equipment list\": read as the Green Jack's, the only hero the PDF gives that list."},
    {"page": 4, "what": "The Fallen Noble is \"0-1 FALLEN NOBLE ... 45 gc each\" and the Hard Men \"35 gc each\"; the prices are each warrior's."}
  ]
}
